        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Generate Email Content Prompt",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const rawPreparedCallToAction =\n  $context?.$nodes?.GENERATE_EMAIL_CONTENT_PROMPT_INPUT?.$output?.result?.preparedCallToAction || {};\n\nconst isStr = (value) => typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() !== \"\";\nconst norm = (value) => (isStr(value) ? value.trim() : \"\");\n\nconst normalizePreparedCallToAction = (value) => ({\n  acknowledgements: norm(value?.acknowledgements ?? value?.updatesBucket?.acknowledgements),\n  defaults: norm(value?.defaults ?? value?.updatesBucket?.defaults),\n  failures: norm(value?.failures ?? value?.failuresBucket?.failures),\n  openIssues: norm(value?.openIssues ?? value?.actionsBucket?.openIssues),\n  recommendations: norm(value?.recommendations ?? value?.actionsBucket?.recommendations),\n  trailingGuidance: norm(value?.trailingGuidance ?? value?.trailingGuidanceBucket?.guidance)\n});\n\nconst preparedCallToAction = Object.fromEntries(\n  Object.entries(normalizePreparedCallToAction(rawPreparedCallToAction)).filter(([, value]) => isStr(value))\n);\nconst preparedCallToActionJson = JSON.stringify(preparedCallToAction, null, 2);\n\nconst defaultMainPrompt = `You are given pre-segmented content for one expense email response.\nYour job is to resolve duplicates/conflicts and produce the final JSON output without rewriting surviving source text.\n\nReturn JSON with exactly:\n{\n  \"callToAction\": \"...\",\n  \"responseTemplate\": \"...\"\n}\n\nInput field definitions (labels only, not source text):\n- These lines describe the input JSON fields only. Never copy these definitions into callToAction or responseTemplate.\n- \"acknowledgements\": confirmed updates already applied\n- \"defaults\": defaulted values already applied\n- \"failures\": restrictive or informational failure content\n- \"openIssues\": unresolved requests for the user\n- \"recommendations\": selectable recommendations for unresolved requests\n- \"trailingGuidance\": app-only guidance that belongs only at the end\n- Missing fields mean the section has no content\n- Do not invent new sections or missing facts\n\nCore rules:\n- Preserve surviving source wording verbatim except duplicated wrapper text\n- Do not paraphrase, soften, summarize, translate, restyle, or rewrite surviving text\n- Preserve all numbers, currency values, policy names, identifiers, field names, and user-facing wording exactly\n- Allowed operations only: reorder sections, remove exact duplicates, remove near-duplicates for the same attribute when one is clearly more specific, choose between conflicting items using the priority rules, group multiple actionable items into a list, trim duplicated wrapper text such as repeated \"Reply with the following for the below expense:\"\n\nConflict priority for the same attribute or requested information:\n1. restrictions or app-only instructions\n2. confirmed updates in acknowledgements or defaults\n3. recommendations\n4. open issues\n\nIf two items at the same priority conflict, keep the more specific one.\nTreat items as the same attribute when they refer to the same field, correction, or choice.\n\nBuild the final callToAction in this order:\n1. acknowledgements, then defaults\n2. failures\n3. resolved open-issues/recommendations section\n4. trailingGuidance\n\nSection-building rules:\n- Merge acknowledgements and defaults without rewriting them\n- Build section 3 from openIssues plus recommendations\n- If a recommendation replaces an open-issue item for the same attribute, drop the matching open-issue item and keep the recommendation.\n- Recommendation-backed actionable items must preserve their selectable-option instruction in section 3; do not collapse them to only the missing field label.\n- For a recommendation-backed item, keep wording equivalent to \"Option 1, 2, or 3 from the below recommendations or enter {missing item}\" so the CTA still carries the option context.\n- Keep surviving open-issue items first and place surviving recommendations after them in section 3\n- Keep only one actionable item per attribute in section 3\n- If any section contains a standalone app-navigation sentence that only directs the user to continue in Oracle Expenses or the Expenses application, treat it as trailingGuidance content instead of section 3 content\n- If a restriction says an attribute cannot be used, will not apply, will be auto-used, or must be completed in the application, do not also ask the user to reply for that same attribute unless both can clearly coexist\n- If acknowledgements/defaults confirm an attribute was already updated, do not ask for that same attribute again unless the inputs clearly show a different unresolved request\n- Do not place trailingGuidance in the middle\n- If trailingGuidance is the only meaningful content, return it as the full callToAction\n\nActionable-content rules:\n- Only the final section 3 content may generate responseTemplate\n- A statement is actionable if it explicitly asks the user to reply, provide, choose, confirm, or enter something\n- A sentence starting with \"Reply with\" is actionable by default\n- If a wrapper sentence introduces a list of requested items, each list item under that wrapper is also actionable unless it is purely informational or app-navigation text\n- Generic status, restriction, navigation, and trailing-guidance text is not actionable\n- If section 3 contains exactly one direct actionable request and there is no stronger conflicting item for the same attribute, keep that request verbatim in callToAction\n- If section 3 comes from a wrapper list and only one requested item survives conflict removal, do not output the bare item label as callToAction; keep the request intent by using the original wrapper with the single surviving item or an equivalent \"Reply with {item} for the below expense.\" sentence\n- Prefer inline text when section 3 has one simple actionable request\n- Use a list only when there are multiple actionable items or selectable options and a list improves readability\n- If section 3 contains exactly one multi-line selectable-options block, preserve that block as-is below any preceding prose; do not wrap it in \"Reply with the following for the below expense:\" and do not create a numbered outer list\n- For a standalone single selectable-options block, preserve its leading \"Reply with\" wording\n- If section 3 contains multiple actionable items or multiple multi-line selectable-options blocks, use the outer \"Reply with the following for the below expense:\" heading and number each top-level item\n- When wrapping a multi-line selectable-options block as a top-level item, use the block heading without the leading \"Reply with\" as the top-level item text and keep that block's numbered options as a nested sublist\n- When section 3 is formatted as a list, strip redundant wrapper text such as leading \"Reply with\" and trailing \"for the below expense\" from each list item while preserving the substantive request text\n- When wrapper text is removed from a list item, also remove any leftover leading article that came only from that wrapper if dropping it makes the item cleaner and more natural\n- In list form, each item should contain only the core request text, not a repeated outer wrapper\n- If section 3 contains multiple actionable items and one item is a multi-line selectable-options block, keep that block intact as a single item and preserve its internal line breaks and numbering\n- When embedding a multi-line selectable-options block inside a larger list, number only the top-level items; keep the selectable block's own numbered options unchanged\n- Preserve useful line breaks\n\nFormatting rules for callToAction:\n- Join consecutive non-list sections into a single paragraph with spaces between sentences instead of line breaks\n- If section 3 is a list, start it on a new paragraph after the preceding prose content\n- Preserve section 3 as a list block when it contains multiple actionable items\n- When section 3 contains multiple actionable items, include the outer heading \"Reply with the following for the below expense:\" immediately before the numbered list\n- If a top-level list item contains a nested selectable-options block, indent each nested option line with four leading spaces\n- trailingGuidance must always be its own final paragraph when other meaningful content exists\n- Do not insert extra blank lines inside a prose paragraph\n- Use blank lines only to separate paragraphs or list blocks\n\nBuild responseTemplate only from the final actionable content in section 3:\n- If section 3 has no actionable content, responseTemplate = \"\"\n- If section 3 has actionable content, callToAction must not be empty\n- responseTemplate is an editable scaffold only; never copy full call-to-action prose into it\n- Each responseTemplate line must contain only the requested entity/value label plus a trailing colon and \"%0A\", except the attached-receipt instruction below\n- Never include \"Reply with\", \"for the below expense\", numbered call-to-action wrappers, or final periods in responseTemplate lines\n- Default format for each final actionable item: \"{requested entity label}:%0A\"\n- For an attached receipt request, use exactly \"Attach a receipt%0A\" with no colon\n- For attendee name/email requests, use exactly \"First Name Last Name, Email:%0A\"\n- For justification or why-over-limit requests, use exactly \"Justification in 240 characters or less:%0A\"\n- For personal amount requests, use exactly \"Personal Receipt Amount:%0A\"\n- For selectable options, use exactly \"Enter option {list numbers}, or enter {missing item}:%0A\"\n- Infer selectable-option responseTemplate lines from the preserved recommendation instruction in callToAction\n- If a selectable-options block starts with a heading followed by numbered options, use the heading text without the trailing colon as {missing item}\n- Treat grouped attendee-choice blocks as selectable options\n- If there are multiple grouped selectable-option blocks, create one responseTemplate line per final actionable block\n- Do not create responseTemplate lines for informational, restrictive, navigational, or trailing-guidance content\n- Capitalize the first character of each responseTemplate line\n\nExamples:\n- If openIssues asks for a field and recommendations provides selectable options for that same field, drop the matching open-issue item and place the recommendation after the remaining open-issue items\n- If acknowledgements, defaults, and failures all survive, combine them into one prose paragraph in that order\n- If section 3 is a list block, place it in a separate paragraph below the prose paragraph\n- If trailingGuidance survives with other content, place it in its own final paragraph\n- If failures is empty, section 3 is empty, and trailingGuidance contains the only text, set callToAction to trailingGuidance and responseTemplate to \"\"\n- If every section is empty, return {\"callToAction\":\"\",\"responseTemplate\":\"\"}\n\nOutput constraints:\n- Output JSON only\n- Do not expose internal section names, metadata, or implementation details\n- Do not add commentary, labels, explanations, or headings`;\n\nconst out = $context?.$nodes?.GET_GENERATE_EMAIL_CONTENT_PROMPT?.$output;\nconst prompts = Array.isArray(out?.prompts) ? out.prompts : [];\nconst mainPrompt = prompts.find((p) => p.promptType === \"MAIN\")?.prompt || defaultMainPrompt;\n\nreturn { mainPrompt, preparedCallToActionJson };"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768518243108"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_GENERATE_EMAIL_CONTENT_PROMPT",
          "id": "1773061031923",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
